  "answer": "Tooth decay starts when the pH of the mouth is lower than 5.5 because tooth enamel, which is made of calcium phosphate, begins to dissolve in acidic conditions. The pH scale measures the concentration of hydrogen ions (H+), and a lower pH indicates a higher concentration of H+ ions, making the environment more acidic. Bacteria in the mouth produce acids by breaking down sugars and food particles, which lowers the pH. When the pH drops below 5.5, the enamel starts to corrode, leading to tooth decay. To prevent this, it is important to clean the mouth after eating and use toothpaste that is basic to neutralize the excess acid.",
